edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column Vector" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1033 1195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "69b57f07-ad86-5963-8f81-f63cb01f239f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050973 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186203956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050973 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186203957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050973 #edb/ref 1031 "Proving a Relation Is an Equivalence Relation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050973 #edb/ref 1033 4942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050973 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "768ca185-f6ef-57ce-96fa-f92273b4f2a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092025 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092025 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](images/22/220e8838850356768215ed74aefc469edbdc99aa50b9116729329f0e818d6978.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2737e6bc-5372-50a0-bf2f-59a91f571a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092025 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=3, y=0, z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=3+0+(-2)=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092026 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092026 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092026 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d32f2604-fc3f-5e80-8085-483e6fd9a3ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092026 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e816a0fcde823bc6f6e88dff0a02c1877275cbed75757c1eb366fb224629127e.svg)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/be/beb80ea3185fc723c294313b63274554ec8af3531ed5643173a6127c59a21bb3.svg)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/e6/e6fac5dd0a9918a03ce7c14e9cd05a06c6d11e95346f261ec75d6ebea09de1d6.svg)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](images/72/72b9d627d372d7a64a271b555b0d4cbb89b2bf9d602cdec64b1d8987a5e21521.svg)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092027 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092027 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d},$ where $A$ and $B$ are $10 \\times 10$ non-singular matrices, while $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are $10 \\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $\\mathbf{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06a50eb4-4976-55fd-aa44-6509b27eccb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092027 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse $B^{−1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d}$ by $B^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{10}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186092025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092185 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092186 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1