 17592186435146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435147 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104515" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435147 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435147 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z=-1 \\\\ 3x-z=5+3y \\\\ 3z-2y=6-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0807a9e2-ba3b-5d6e-8562-a580bc61f62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435147 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z=-1 \\\\ 3x-3y-z=5 \\\\ x-2y+3z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-9-2)-(9+1)-2(-6+3) \\\\  & =-22-10+6 \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 26 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=1-1+1=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78565" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,x=A\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c58ffa5-e4d4-5bf5-8b35-8a71f48534ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435148 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x=A\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z=3 \\\\ x-2y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-y+2z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e321af2f-d67a-5dc4-a077-c6060845ea99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435149 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=1,z=4.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=-1+1+4=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
